# Google Maps API Configuration
# Get your API key from: https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis/credentials

VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=AIzaSyDXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# ========================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ========================================

# 1. Get API Key:
#    - Go to: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#    - Click "Create Credentials" → "API Key"
#    - Copy the key and replace the value above

# 2. Enable Required APIs:
#    Go to: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library
#    Enable these APIs:
#    ✓ Maps JavaScript API
#    ✓ Places API  
#    ✓ Geocoding API
#    ✓ Directions API

# 3. Configure API Key Restrictions:
#    Go to: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#    Click on your API key → Edit
#    
#    Application restrictions:
#    - Select: HTTP referrers (websites)
#    - Add these referrers:
#      http://localhost:5173/*
#      http://127.0.0.1:5173/*
#      http://localhost:3000/*
#      http://127.0.0.1:3000/*
#      https://yourdomain.com/*
#    
#    API restrictions:
#    - Select: Restrict key
#    - Choose:
#      ✓ Maps JavaScript API
#      ✓ Places API
#      ✓ Geocoding API
#      ✓ Directions API
#    
#    Click "Save"

# 4. Enable Billing:
#    - Google Maps requires billing enabled
#    - Free tier: $200/month credit
#    - Go to: https://console.cloud.google.com/billing

# 5. After setup:
#    - Copy this file to .env.local
#    - Replace the API key with your real key
#    - Restart dev server: npm run dev

# ========================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ========================================

# InvalidKeyMapError:
# - Check API key is correct (no spaces)
# - Verify all 4 APIs are enabled
# - Check HTTP referrers include localhost:5173
# - Wait 5 minutes after creating/updating key
# - Enable billing in Google Cloud Console

# Autocomplete not showing:
# - Check browser console for errors
# - Verify .env.local file exists
# - Ensure server was restarted after adding .env.local
# - Check z-index in DevTools (dropdown should be visible)
